    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `GOLD` membership tier rule: an owner's tier becomes `GOLD` when their household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) has 3+ members after the create; otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules still apply.\n\nFollowing the project's existing pattern for derived-at-create fields like `namesakeCount`, the household size is computed during the `POST /api/owners` pipeline, frozen onto the entity, and read back by the mapper:\n\n1. **New function** `CountOwnerHousehold.java` \u2014 runs after `AssignOwnerHousehold` (so the shared `householdId` is set and existing members are backfilled) and before `SaveOwner` (so the new owner isn't yet persisted). It counts existing owners carrying the same `householdId` and adds 1 for the owner being created, storing it as `householdSize`. An owner that didn't opt into a household has no `householdId` and counts as a household of one.\n\n2. **Pipeline wiring** \u2014 inserted the `countHousehold` step into `owners.POST.yml` with `govern: [ transaction ]`, matching the surrounding steps.\n\n3. **Entity** `Owner.java` \u2014 added the `householdSize` field (`household_size` column) with getter/setter.\n\n4. **Schemas** \u2014 added `household_size INTEGER` to all four DB schemas (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres).\n\n5. **Mapper** `OwnerMapper.membershipTier` \u2014 returns `GOLD` when `householdSize >= 3`, otherwise falls through to the unchanged SILVER/BRONZE logic.\n\n6. **openapi.yml** \u2014 updated the `membershipTier` description to document the GOLD rule.",
